 ],
 "literal": "Excellent-headed palmyra palm's tender great leaf-stalks, / with beautiful bells and a large garland, according to tradition having fastened, / white bones having worn, so that others mock, having appeared, / within the span of one day, casting away great modesty, / even to walk in the street, will it indeed bring? / The proudly shining, swaying-gaited innocent girl, / she did not grow thin, for us to send the appropriate messenger.",
 "translation": "Will my love indeed bring me to cast away my great modesty in a single day, and walk the streets riding a horse made of tender, large palmyra leaf-stalks from the fine-headed palm tree, decorated with beautiful bells and a large garland according to custom, wearing white bones while others mock? That innocent girl of proud, shining, swaying gait has not relented or grown thin, so that we might send a proper messenger.",
 "modern": "சிறந்த உச்சியைக் கொண்ட பனைமரத்தின் இளமையான பெரிய மடல் குதிரையை, அழகிய மணிகள் பூட்டிய பெரிய மாலையோடு மரபுப்படி கட்டி, வெண்மையான எலும்புகளை அணிந்துகொண்டு மற்றவர்கள் எள்ளி நகையாடுமாறு தெருவில் தோன்றி, ஒரே நாளில் எனது பெரிய நாணத்தை விடுத்துத் தெருவில் உலா வரச் செய்யுமோ? பெருமிதமும் ஒளியும் கொண்ட அசைந்து நடக்கும் நடையுடைய அந்தப் பேதை, நாம் தூது அனுப்புவதற்கு ஏற்றவாறு மெலிவடையவில்லை.",
 "explanation": "The hero is speaking to himself or his friend in a state of deep distress because his love is unfulfilled. He contemplates riding the 'maṭal'—a mock horse made of rough palmyra stems—to publicize his love and force the heroine's family to agree to their marriage. This desperate act involves abandoning all shame in a single day, wearing bones, and riding through the streets while being mocked by onlookers. He laments that the heroine, with her beautiful swaying gait, has not grown thin with longing or shown any pity. Because she remains unaffected, sending a conventional messenger to plead his case would be entirely useless.",
 "model": "gemini-3.5-flash",
 "generated": "2026-11-26"
}